I got the quest from Auberdine, and as soon as I got it, started looking for a party for BFD.&nbsp; I generally don't lookup quests on Thottbot unless I REALLY get stuck so not knowing exactly where the gem dropped and assuming it would drop from one boss or another in the instance&nbsp; I got together a full party and did the entire instance (looting the Naga all the way into and through the instance),&nbsp; By the time we got to the main boss I was getting a little worried and sure enough at the end of the instance I still had no Kor Gem...
I read the Thottbot posts on the subject and realised that I didn't need to do the instance at all...&nbsp; but still I had looted every Naga I could on the way in.&nbsp; I hearthed out and came back alone, about 2 Naga in the Kor Gem dropped.&nbsp; 
My conclusion: despite the paladin quest saying that the items are listed in order of dificulty to attain (leading me to believe it must be in the instance, this is definitely soloable for a paly (I was lvl 23 at the time but I think it could be done at 20 with careful pulling and some skill as a paly) and should be done solo to guarantee that the Gem drops quickly.
The long and the short of it [b]SOLO THIS QUEST AS SOON AS YOU CAN[/b] and get your mace at lvl 20 or as close to as possible&nbsp;

