There may be a bit of confusion related to the earliest comments regarding "talking to the banker".&nbsp; I think this may have occurred while the person was trying to turn in one of several quests that were completed in Uldaman, specifically, "The Platinum Discs" which you complete at the end of the Dungeon after you kill Boss Archaedas.
&nbsp; 
While in the Uldaman Cave or Dungeon Instance,&nbsp; (s)he most likely picked up "The Shattered Necklace" and kept playing. (You can only pick up one, because they start a new quest, but they are dropped randomly by many of the opponents so that everyone can get one.)
&nbsp; 
When (s)he got to the Vault to turn in "The Platinum Discs" quest to Vault Administrator Dinita Stonemantle, part of the reward was a 14 slot Thawpelt Sack.
&nbsp; 
When (s)he completed the disc quest and got the sack reward, (s)he most likely opened her/his pack and looked for that new sack.&nbsp; That's probably when (s)he realized that (s)he had the necklace that starts another quest.
&nbsp; 
When (s)he right clicked on it, it told him/her to find out who TdK is.&nbsp; 

The banker doesn't have anything to do with either quest, except maybe to allow you to withdraw 5 silver bars from your bank bag if you ask nicely.
&nbsp; 
That is the point at which you need to get 5 Silver Bars so you can pay them to TdK so he will tell you about the next part of The Shattered Necklace quest.&nbsp; 

Simple, eh?&nbsp; Really nice Exp when you do it in that sequence.

