Me, (lvl 59, several greens, combat spec) and another rogue, (60, mostly blues, also combat spec), duo'd the mob that drops the hammer necessary for the key.&nbsp; Using Zero260's excellent instructions we got to a room with tons of "Wrath hammer Constructs" We killed the one that is by the top of the ramp, (ramp goes down north from the door, then takes a 90 degree turn west, again heading down, then takes another 90 degree turn south creating an up side down U.&nbsp; You will enter on the right side of the upside down U)&nbsp; There are also some dwarven workers in an alcove to the right, 3, be careful not to aggro them when killing the first stationary Construct, as they hit hard even though non elite.&nbsp; 

After you kill the dwarves, there is a patrolling Construct.&nbsp; Kill him, and now you should have most of the right part of the upside down U to yourselves (the part before it begins to turn into a ramp)&nbsp; Look across, and you should see Fineous Darkvire at the bottom of the left side of the upside down U.&nbsp; He will stand there for quite a while, but eventually if you wait, (5-10 minutes by my estimate, its a while, be patient)&nbsp; He walks up the ramp to where you cleared the stationary, and patrolling construct, and the dwarven workers.&nbsp; Here you begin your battle.&nbsp; 

I cant say exactly the best way to beat him, but basically my buddy got aggro first, and we brought him down as far as possible.&nbsp; He used evasion and a major health pot.&nb

The only spawns I've run into are

1) Spawns when all the Relic Coffers are opened;
2) A spawn in a different area (the hallway towards the patrolling named and a bunch of golems) of a few non-named and one named when the portrait is opened.

I killed approximately 225 Trappers at and around 38,38 the droprate is far from 90% in fact it is almost exactly 7% at that location I got 2 for every 30 I killed.&nbsp; I'm not making this up since with cosmos you can now see the exact droprate that you have experienced, and I would think that after getting 15 Bloodpetals at a 2/30 droprate that I would have a significant sample size.&nbsp; 

I found a possibly better location a little further north at 40,23; I do not know the droprate on these since I got to them when I had 14/15 Bloodpetals, but they are Trappers and there are a lot of them in a much smaller proximity as opposed to the nightmarishly far apart ones at 38,38.&nbsp; Here's hoping they drop decent, even if they don't you'll fare better than you would at 38,38.&nbsp; 

Please keep in mind guys that if you kill one and get one drop, the droprate is not 100%.&nbsp; Or say you got 12/15 by killing somewhere with a really low droprate, then you decided to check somewhere else, you kill 4 more and get your last 3.&nbsp; This doesn't mean the droprate on the new place/enemy is 75%, it could just mean you got lucky.&nbsp;

