if he is in the area, he'll be targeted and you can map your path by picking only those mobs that are in the way.&nbsp; 

Btw, he aggros a fair bit and you may end up having to kill 2 or 3.&nbsp; Just watch out.&nbsp; Also watch out for the troop of horde that is circling this small mountain going from camp to camp.&nbsp; They got me good once.&nbsp;

Ok, you need to get through two doors to get into the Library., so a Crescent Key or two charges or lockpicking are needed.

[b]Enter DM North[/b].&nbsp; There is a left-right pathway overlooking a courtyard ahead of you.&nbsp; There is a mob with dogs who walks down there (in a circle, so you can go after him) and another one who walks to the ramp and back (so wait until he is heading away from the ramp).&nbsp; Avoid those!&nbsp; 

When the coast is clear, go forward toward the courtyard and turn left.&nbsp; Almost immediately on your right is a ramp heading down into the courtyard.&nbsp; 

You need to jump up on the left wall of the ramp.&nbsp; To do this you need to achieve a certain velocity and angle so it may take a couple tries, but it's not too tricky.&nbsp; [i]You cannot walk down this ramp into the courtyard because you will draw aggro from 4 elites.[/i]&nbsp; Likewise, when you are coming back up you will definitely draw aggro unless you have some clever tricks at your disposal.&nbsp; 

From the wall jump down on the grass and walk toward the other ramp, which heads west. This ramp has another locked door at the bottom which leads to a tunnel going to the Library.&nbsp; When you open the door there's a long tunnel going straight there - no aggro at all.&nbsp; 

[b]The NPC for Elven Legends is a skeleton on the floor next to Lorekeeper Lydros.[/b]&nbsp; Interact with the skeleton, return to the quest giver in Feathermoon and you're good to go for the Libram quests.

